        "solution": "<b>Solution (EN):</b><br>Let the original number be x.<br>Given increase percentage = 247<sup>1</sup>/<sub>2</sub>% = 495/2 %<br><br>According to the question, the total increment is 990:<br>x &times; (495 / (2 &times; 100)) = 990<br>x &times; (99 / 40) = 990<br>x = 990 &times; (40 / 99)<br>x = 10 &times; 40 = 400<br><br>The original number is 400.<br>Therefore, the number of zeros at the end of the original number is 2.<br><br><b>Solution (HI):</b><br>माना मूल संख्या x है।<br>दी गई वृद्धि प्रतिशत = 247<sup>1</sup>/<sub>2</sub>% = 495/2 %<br><br>प्रश्नानुसार, कुल वृद्धि 990 है:<br>x &times; (495 / (2 &times; 100)) = 990<br>x &times; (99 / 40) = 990<br>x = 990 &times; (40 / 99)<br>x = 10 &times; 40 = 400<br><br>मूल संख्या 400 है।<br>अतः मूल संख्या के अंत में शून्यों की संख्या 2 है।<br><br><b>Fraction Method:</b><br>247<sup>1</sup>/<sub>2</sub>% = 200% + 47.5% = 2 + 19/40 = 99/40<br>Here, the numerator (99 units) represents the increment, and the denominator (40 units) represents the original number.<br>99 units = 990 &rArr; 1 unit = 10<br>Original number = 40 units = 40 &times; 10 = 400<br>Number of trailing zeros in 400 = 2."
