        "q_en": "Study the given graph and answer the question that follows.<br>The following graph depicts the number of persons who purchased four different products (A, B, C and D) in two consecutive years (2001 and 2002).<br><br><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEhjKs5J_Wwdbsl_8C98Pu5viiK4UbZEj4z53cZtJkF6vOI56yqXAviSvxVwMXiSHTWG2_SCErzI_dh3V6A0FLCVQXEF1rLP3Ewuk8RE3Jl5zU8W7erA-rxJpp1VnePsPpWF5BOPhhE4PAw-J-AozXx0A4raSI5LkKfqVOvvdhMo60AiyJhOK_yv8kkyBxM=rw\" style=\"height: auto; max-width: 100%;\"><br><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\"><span style=\"tab-stops: 75.95pt;\"><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\"><span style=\"font-family: Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">What is the ratio of the number of persons who have purchased the products A and B together in 2001 to the number of persons who have purchased the product C in 2002?</span></span></span></span>",
